{"_v":1,"id":"cabaret-at-the-kit-kat-club-west-end-2021","bd":{"positive":9,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Clive Davis","o":"The Times (UK)","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/cabaret-review-sinister-redmayne-and-sumptuous-set-are-a-seductive-combination-8r76crq0g","d":"2023-06-16","q":"Liza Sadovy's doomed romance with Elliot Levey's Jewish lodger, Herr Schultz, comes close to eclipsing Sally and Cliff."},{"cn":"Patrick Marmion","o":"Daily Mail","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.dailymail.co.uk/tvshowbiz/article-10302945/At-Eddies-Cabaret-sets-wunderbar-PATRICK-MARMION-reviews-Cabaret.html","d":"2021-12-13","q":"Tom Scutt's astonishing makeover of the Playhouse Theatre: Transforming the West End venue into a very swanky speakeasy."},{"cn":"Quentin Letts","o":"The Times (UK)","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/cabaret-is-amazing-but-eddie-redmayne-is-miscast-nxsnxvczb","d":"2021-12-19","q":"Cabaret looks terrific, sounds pretty good and retains its powerful \"live and let live\" message."},{"cn":"Alexandra Pollard","o":"The Independent","s":93,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/cabaret-review-jessie-buckley-eddie-redmayne-b1974565.html","d":"2021-12-13","q":"Perhaps the best musical-theatre performance I have ever seen live is Buckley's rendition of the title song."},{"cn":"Sarah Crompton","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":89,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/london-theatre/reviews/cabaret-eddie-redmayne-buckley-west-end_55529.html","d":"2021-12-12","q":"The result is both shattering and utterly magnificent."},{"cn":"Suzy Evans","o":"London Theatre","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/cabaret-at-the-kit-kat-club-review-eddie-redmayne-and-jessie-buckley","d":"2021-12-13","q":"The Kit Kat Club is the ultimate escape."},{"cn":"Tim Bano","o":"The Stage","s":87,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/long-reviews/cabaret-review-eddie-redmayne-jessie-buckley-kit-kat-club-london-2021-rebecca-frecknall","d":"2021-12-13","q":"Every decision [Frecknall] makes here has clear, clever purpose."},{"cn":"Fiona Mountford","o":"The i","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://inews.co.uk/culture/arts/cabaret-playhouse-theatre-review-eddie-redmayne-jessie-buckley-omari-douglas-is-chilling-dark-stripped-back-1347474","d":"2021-12-13","q":"That one moment, the shattering of those small but universal dreams, tells us everything we need to know."},{"cn":"David Nice","o":"The Arts Desk","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://theartsdesk.com/theatre/cabaret-kit-kat-club-playhouse-theatre-review-%E2%80%93-polymorphous-prodigious","d":"2021-12-13","q":"This is an experience well up to the standards of the very best you'd pay a lot for at Glyndebourne or the Royal Opera."},{"cn":"Theatre Bee (UK)","o":"Theatre Bee","s":64,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://www.theatrebee.com/post/review-cabaret-at-the-kit-kat-club","d":"2022-06-02","q":"In all, the songs were lovely, the musical was thought-provoking, albeit a little difficult to piece together for a complete newbie."}],"au":{"score":92,"designation":"Loving","sources":{"mz":{"s":92,"c":5135,"sr":4.6}}}}